Notes
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- The zip files are read directly with geopandas, no need to unzip.
- weather_<region>_<year>.parquet files are local backups made by
  Oblig3.ipynb. They are not raw data and not in git. Each row is one
  hour in one ERA5 grid cell. n_points says how many of the 100 random
  locations in the region fell in that cell (see src/ind320/openmeteo.py
  for why the download is done per grid cell).
- NVE data is licensed under NLOD / CC BY 4.0 (credit: NVE).
  Open-Meteo data is CC BY 4.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
grid_cells.csv
--------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     Derived, but static. One row per area and ERA5 grid cell:
          area_type, area_nr, latitude, longitude, n_points.
          n_points = how many of the area's random locations fell in
          the cell (its weight when averaging over the area).
Made by:  Oblig3.ipynb (areas.save_grid_cells), from the three
          shapefiles above, 100 random locations per area, seed 320,
          snapped to the 0.25° ERA5 grid.
Used by:  The Streamlit app and the weather download, so neither has
          to repeat the sampling. Same inputs give the same file.